WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
Whose marketing is better,

00:00:01.141 --> 00:00:04.381
Lemme or Goalie? Lemme is running 380 active Facebook ads.

00:00:04.382 --> 00:00:07.501
They are advertising in multiple languages to reach mass markets.

00:00:07.502 --> 00:00:09.501
They are also running paid collaboration ads

00:00:09.502 --> 00:00:13.301
because they know those can outperform traditional ads by 15 to 30%.

00:00:13.302 --> 00:00:16.301
That is a massive lift. And they combine celebrity credibility,

00:00:16.302 --> 00:00:18.381
full brand breakdowns, and endless U G. C.

00:00:18.382 --> 00:00:19.461
But then you look at Goalie.

00:00:19.462 --> 00:00:22.621
Goalie is running 3,000 active Facebook ads. 3,000?

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.421
That is absolutely ridiculous.

00:00:24.422 --> 00:00:27.021
It is nearly 10 times limits volume at that point.

00:00:27.022 --> 00:00:28.501
They are not testing a few formats,

00:00:28.502 --> 00:00:30.581
they are testing practically every format,

00:00:30.582 --> 00:00:31.561
angle, hook,

00:00:31.562 --> 00:00:33.261
audience, and offer imaginable.

00:00:33.262 --> 00:00:35.261
Lemmy sends traffic to custom product pages

00:00:35.262 --> 00:00:37.581
focused heavily on subscriptions only. Why?

00:00:37.582 --> 00:00:39.261
Because they do not want one purchase.

00:00:39.262 --> 00:00:41.541
They want the customer paying every single month,

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:44.021
increasing retention and lifetime value at scale.

00:00:44.022 --> 00:00:46.221
Goalie takes an entirely different approach.

00:00:46.222 --> 00:00:47.221
They lead with bundles

00:00:47.222 --> 00:00:49.581
designed to get customers buying more of their products

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:52.101
in the very first order. That drives higher AOV,

00:00:52.102 --> 00:00:52.941
stronger ROAS,

00:00:52.942 --> 00:00:55.221
and gives them more room to flood the market with ad spend.

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:57.861
Now TikTok Shop is where this gets completely insane.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.340
has over 19,000 affiliates who have posted more than 86,000 videos,

00:01:02.341 --> 00:01:05.541
and they went from zero to $20 million in only a few months

00:01:05.542 --> 00:01:08.661
on TikTok Shop. That level of growth is almost unheard of.

00:01:08.662 --> 00:01:11.101
Goalie's numbers are even harder to comprehend.

00:01:11.102 --> 00:01:15.101
They have generated over $146 million on TikTok Shop.

00:01:15.102 --> 00:01:19.981
87,000 creators with more than 662,000 Videos posted.

00:01:19.982 --> 00:01:22.061
That is nearly eight videos per creator.

00:01:22.062 --> 00:01:23.761
It's absolutely mind blowing.

00:01:23.762 --> 00:01:26.861
Both brands understand that TikTok Shop is not just a sales channel.

00:01:26.862 --> 00:01:29.501
It is a massive distribution engine that lifts retail,

00:01:29.502 --> 00:01:30.141
paid ads,

00:01:30.142 --> 00:01:33.461
brand awareness in the entire marketing ecosystem all together.

00:01:33.462 --> 00:01:35.141
So whose marketing is actually better?

00:01:35.142 --> 00:01:36.581
Lemme. Who's taking off right now?

00:01:36.582 --> 00:01:38.903
Or goalie who's become an absolute giant?
